---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {edition,stops,stopURL} from '../lib/catalog';
---
<Layout title="Saint Paul After Dark"><div class="container">
 <section class="home-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">1900–1938 · Seven chapters</p><h1>SAINT PAUL <br/>AFTER DARK</h1><p class="lede">{edition.tagline}</p><p>Follow the bargain that offered criminals refuge, the people who carried its costs, and the records that complicate the legend.</p><div class="controls"><a class="btn" href="/prologue/">Start the tour</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/map/">Explore the seven stops</a></div><p><a data-resume hidden href="/map/">Resume reading</a></p></div><figure><img src="/media/scenes/scene-skyline.svg" width="1200" height="700" alt="Generalized noir skyline illustration, not a surveyed view of Saint Paul." fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>Reconstruction · An illustrative setting, not historical evidence.</figcaption></figure></section>
 <section class="prose"><h2>Read the city through its evidence</h2><p>This is a self-paced reading tour for home use. The complete text is available without sound. Each chapter separates historical accounts, records, and interpretation; disputed stories retain their qualifications.</p><p>{edition.contentNote}</p><p>There are no timers or scores. Use a keyboard, voice commands matching the visible button labels, or ordinary links. Calm view reduces decoration and turns ambience off. Progress is saved locally when your browser permits it.</p></section>
 <section><h2>The reading order</h2><ol class="chapter-grid">{stops.map(s=><li class="card"><p class="eyebrow">{s.period}</p><h3><a href={stopURL(s.id)}>{s.title}</a></h3><p>{s.synopsis}</p><span class="muted" data-visited-stop={s.id} data-js-control hidden></span></li>)}</ol></section>
</div></Layout>
